  "optionAName": "Pension Lump Sum",
  "optionBName": "Pension Annuity (Monthly Payments)",
  "introText": "A monthly pension annuity gives you a guaranteed income stream with the investment and longevity risk on your plan, while a lump sum hands you the full value to roll over and invest yourself, which gives flexibility and the chance of higher or lower total wealth. At ModernWallet, we review retirement decisions through the lens of long-term cash flow, and choosing between these two payout structures determines who manages your market risk for the rest of your life. The two paths are mutually exclusive once your election window closes. Every worker facing a pension buyout or retirement distribution must balance predictable lifetime payments against control over invested assets.",
